==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From a derivative of {{etyl|la|pt}} {{term|cor||heart|lang=la}} with the suffix {{term|-ção|-ação|lang=pt}}, either a {{etyl|VL.|pt}} root *''coratione'' or *''coraceone''. Compare Spanish {{term|corazón|lang=es}}, Mozarabic ''[[quračún]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Brazil}} {{IPA|[ko.ɾaˈsɐ̃w̃]|lang=pt}}
* {{a|Portugal}} {{IPA|[ku.ɾɐˈsãw̃]|lang=pt}}
*: {{audio|pt-pt-coração.ogg|Audio (PT)}}

